## Summary

Investigated Eliza’s winter party sharing error with production data, request logs and Chrome. Her existing Hawks/Falcons Winter Party at https://when.heliosian.com/g/halcons-winter-skate had working host controls and guest rules for Hawks, Hawks parents, Falcons and Falcons parents. No production repair was needed, and 126 pending invitations were left unsent.

Before: event and saved-calendar creation misread the write API response as an array and reported failure after saving.
Now: both callers read the response’s result array and complete with the saved row’s ID.

Before: retrying creation with an existing event address could mask duplicate-address validation with a missing-group error because writes and triggers used an earlier model after validation failed.
Now: ordinary writes and staged triggers preserve model validation errors and roll back refused creation.

Kept the shared API contract and corrected the two calendar callers. Regression tests cover duplicate-address HTTP 400, atomic rollback and successful full creation retry. Chrome verified event creation, duplicate-address handling and saved-calendar creation. Focused database/store tests and repository-wide go vet passed; the full database suite reached its required 30-second limit. Review returned no findings.

Checked Ian’s alternative explanation of invite-group rule editing. The screenshot’s Share the event label is exclusive to creation, and production request sizes matched creation; failed request bodies were not logged. Local rule preview found 22 people, and adding and saving the rule both succeeded. No additional rule-path defect was found.

No schema edits, production writes or invitation sends. Merged main into the task branch without conflicts or substantive resolutions, leaving the merge uncommitted for byre to conclude.

